        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Fishing Shack setup and a long but repeatable fishing/friendship farm.\n\n1. Unlock the Garrison Fishing Shack and train Draenor Fishing. For the level 3 blueprint earn Draenor Angler by catching 100 Enormous fish of each of its seven required types: Abyssal Gulper, Blackwater Whiptail, Blind Lake Sturgeon, Fat Sleeper, Fire Ammonite, Jawless Skulker and Sea Scorpion. Fish in their matching Draenor zones; Sea Scorpion is coastal. An account blueprint unlock need not be re-earned on every alt.\n\n2. Upgrade the Fishing Shack to level 3 and reach 100 effective Draenor Fishing. Take Luring Nat from Segumi (Alliance) or Rak'jin (Horde). Catch the requested Arcane Trout in Shadowmoon Valley or Molten Catfish in Frostfire Ridge, then hand it in.\n\n3. Take Finding Nat Pagle to Nat at Anglers Wharf in Krasarang Wilds (68.4,43.4). Accept The Great Angler Returns BEFORE leaving Pandaria and return to your Fishing Shack. Keep your fishing equipment/lure on if dropping below 100 skill hides the follow-up.\n\n4. Complete A True Draenor Angler when offered: use Nat's supplied lure and catch the six requested zone lunkers, then return them. Finish An Angler on Our Team to recruit him. The attached quest route keeps the recruitment stages separate from ordinary repeatable lunker hand-ins.\n\n5. Fish lunkers and turn them in to Nat at the Garrison Shack for friendship and one Nat's Lucky Coin each. Useful spots include the river under the bridge at 64.3,21.9 in Spires of Arak and Felmouth Frenzy pools along the fel river at 42.5,49.4 in Tanaan. Pool and open-water catches both work; no old five-lunker carry limit applies.\n\n6. Continue until Nat's friendship says Best Friend AND you have 100 coins. Optional Pandaria rare-fish dailies also raise his friendship, but do not replace the coin requirement. Reserve the coins rather than spending them on his other rewards.\n\n7. Buy Reins of the Crimson Water Strider from Nat at your Garrison Fishing Shack, use the item and check the Mount Journal.",
