        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - A capture chase and several daily training stages; combat is easy at high level.\n\n1. Build a Stables on a large Garrison plot. Level 1 is enough for the six trained mounts. Enable trivial-quest tracking and speak to Keegan Firebeard / Fanny Firebeard in Lunarfall, or Tormak the Scarred / Sage Paluna in Frostwall. The Stables' position depends on your chosen plot.\n\n2. Accept Entangling an Elekk at the Stables. Capture introductions unlock over successive days; if this beast is not offered yet, complete the introductions already available and return after the daily reset.\n\n3. Lasso a Young Meadowstomper north of Wor'var. Follow the side path around its rock-bridge jump instead of trying to copy the jump. Use an ordinary mount for the chase, not a Nagrand outpost vehicle.\n\n4. Return the capture quest to the Stables. On each following day accept the next Elekk Training quest. The attached character route lists every training quest and points to your next unfinished pickup, objective or hand-in.\n\n5. At each named target use the supplied Meadowstomper-In-Training Whistle BEFORE fighting. Remain on that training beast for kill credit. A normal Mount Journal summon is not the training vehicle; pets or companions that dismount you can spoil credit.\n\n6. Work through the route in order: Cruel Ogres, Darkwing Roc, Moth of Wrath, Thundercall, Ironbore, Orc Hunters, The Garn. Hand each quest in and wait for the next daily offer rather than killing all targets on day one.\n\n7. After The Garn, return to the Stables and finish the hand-in. Learn Trained Meadowstomper from the reward / check the Mount Journal. The earned mount remains yours if you later replace the Stables building. If trainers stop showing daily quests, try logging out and back in while standing inside the Stables.",
    },
    [171624] = {
        category = "Garrison",
        mountCategory = "Rare Drops",
        sourceType = "Rare Drops",
        source = "Gold/Platinum Garrison invasion bags and invasion bosses",
