            },
            { mapID = 543, x = 0.5, y = 0.27, step = 2, label = "Iron Siegeworks - provoke an invasion" },
        },
        reviewedAt = "2026-11-14",
        itemId = 116663,
        name = "Shadowhide Pearltusk",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=116663",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Weekly character rewards and low random drops, including duplicates.\n\n1. Return to your level 3 Garrison and check whether an invasion is already pending from Sergeant Crowler (Alliance) or Sergeant Grimjaw (Horde). Enable trivial-quest tracking so the offer is visible.\n\n2. If no invasion is pending, buy a Scouting Missive for an assault such as the Iron Siegeworks. Complete the assault and keep killing the associated Draenor enemies until their invasion triggers. One missive is not guaranteed to trigger it immediately. Return and hand in the missive, then check the sergeant again.\n\n3. Start the invasion and actively defend: kill waves quickly, rescue frightened citizens, intercept saboteurs and defend buildings. Move between entry points instead of camping one attacker. Helpers can cover different lanes.\n\n4. Reach at least 1,000 points for Gold and aim for 1,300 for Platinum. Continue through the final event/boss after the timer; final-wave points can push the score over the threshold.\n\n5. Open Invader's Forgotten Treasure and, for Platinum, Invader's Abandoned Sack. Each can contain any of the four invasion mounts and duplicates are possible. If a bag contains a boss-summoning item, use its Garrison invasion-boss event for an additional loot opportunity.\n\n6. Learn Shadowhide Pearltusk if awarded. Otherwise repeat the eligible Gold/Platinum reward farm after the weekly reset, or do it on other characters with invasion access. Optional Festive Outfits from Winter Veil can improve guards on some versions, but are not required for this farm.",
    },
