        mountCategory = "Achievements",
        sourceType = "Achievements",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Stables upgrades, six trained/captured beasts and thirty-six deliberate kill credits.\n\n1. Capture all six beasts using the level 1 Stables introductions. Upgrade the Stables to level 3; the level 3 blueprint unlock comes from Master of Mounts after completing all six training chains. Pick up Garn-Tooth Necklace from inside the building and finish its short conversation quest if offered.\n\n2. Get all six mount-in-training whistles. If the daily chains are already finished, ask Keegan Firebeard (Alliance) or Tormak the Scarred (Horde) for replacement whistles; finishing a chain does not permanently lock you out of this achievement.\n\n3. Put Garn-Tooth Necklace in your character's bags and keep it there. It weakens/slows the training mount. Open The Stable Master in the achievement panel and track its six target counters.\n\n4. Visit Gorian Beast-Lasher (79.2,71.6), Thundercall (90.6,23.6), Ironbore (53.2,77.6), Karak the Great Hunter (69.0,34.3), Maimclaw (63.0,80.0), and Moth of Wrath (43.0,69.1), all in Draenor Nagrand. At EACH target use a different whistle and kill it once on every training beast: talbuk, clefthoof, boar, riverbeast, elekk and wolf. Wait for respawns between kills.\n\n5. That is 36 separate credits. Remain on the training vehicle for every kill; normal mounts do not count. If one counter is short, repeat that target with the missing beast rather than restarting the whole route.\n\n6. When the achievement completes, check the Mount Journal for Armored Frostwolf. The reward is automatic. You can bank the modifier after all required credits are recorded.",
    },
