        tips = "",
        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - A capture chase and several daily training stages; combat is easy at high level.\n\n1. Build a Stables on a large Garrison plot. Level 1 is enough for the six trained mounts. Enable trivial-quest tracking and speak to Keegan Firebeard / Fanny Firebeard in Lunarfall, or Tormak the Scarred / Sage Paluna in Frostwall. The Stables' position depends on your chosen plot.\n\n2. Accept Wrangling a Wolf at the Stables. Capture introductions unlock over successive days; if this beast is not offered yet, complete the introductions already available and return after the daily reset.\n\n3. Take the path at 58.2,64.8 onto Shadowfall Canyon, east of Oshu'gun. Lasso a Young Snarler and follow its jumps between rock islands. Retry the capture if a fall breaks the rope; avoid the Nagrand outpost mount.\n\n4. Return the capture quest to the Stables. On each following day accept the next Wolf Training quest. The attached character route lists every training quest and points to your next unfinished pickup, objective or hand-in.\n\n5. At each named target use the supplied Snarler-In-Training Whistle BEFORE fighting. Remain on that training beast for kill credit. A normal Mount Journal summon is not the training vehicle; pets or companions that dismount you can spoil credit.\n\n6. Work through the route in order: Cruel Ogres, Darkwing Roc, Moth of Wrath, Thundercall, Ironbore, Orc Hunters, The Garn. Hand each quest in and wait for the next daily offer rather than killing all targets on day one.\n\n7. After The Garn, return to the Stables and finish the hand-in. Learn Trained Snarler from the reward / check the Mount Journal. The earned mount remains yours if you later replace the Stables building. If trainers stop showing daily quests, try logging out and back in while standing inside the Stables.",
